Third-party software
--------------------
Linux client (linux/), built with the openmcx-server sources and their libraries (see openmcx-server NOTICE):

  wolfSSL 5.8.2            GPL-3.0-or-later         https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssl
  pjproject (PJSIP) 2.17   GPL-2.0-or-later         https://github.com/pjsip/pjproject
  libsrtp2                 BSD-3-Clause             https://github.com/cisco/libsrtp
  OpenH264                 BSD-2-Clause             https://github.com/cisco/openh264
  opencore-amr, vo-amrwbenc  Apache-2.0             https://sourceforge.net/projects/opencore-amr/
  nlohmann/json, libxml2   MIT                      https://github.com/nlohmann/json, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2
  OpenSSL 3                Apache-2.0               https://www.openssl.org

Dispatcher (dispatcher/):

  Go standard library      BSD-3-Clause             https://go.dev
  golang.org/x/net         BSD-3-Clause             https://go.googlesource.com/net
  and the Linux client above, as its engine

Android app (android/), libraries pinned in android/gradle/libs.versions.toml:

  Kotlin standard library, kotlinx.coroutines, kotlinx.serialization
                           Apache-2.0               https://github.com/JetBrains
  AndroidX (core, core-telecom, lifecycle, activity, browser, Compose, Material 3)
                           Apache-2.0               https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx
  zxing-android-embedded and ZXing
                           Apache-2.0               https://github.com/journeyapps/zxing-android-embedded
  The app uses Android's own AMR-WB and H.264 codecs (MediaCodec); it bundles no codec.
